  "id": "symptomatic-treatment",
  "term": "symptomatic treatment",
  "definition": "Symptomatic treatment is care aimed at reducing a condition’s visible symptoms rather than addressing the underlying disease process or biological mechanism. In this context, it is contrasted with mechanism-based approaches that target the causes of the disorder itself.",
